        <body>
            <div xml:id="d55">

                <pb facs="0193" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg81"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 23700/7.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Beaupré to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The
                            Hague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-03-31"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">March 31, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Beaupré says he is notified by the Luxemburg Government of the arrest made in
                    compliance with the telegraphic request of Wood, detective captain, of Chicago,
                    at Luxemburg on March 24 of Nicholas Knepper on charge of larceny. Asks if
                    extradition papers are being sent t-o the legation.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
